# A Structure of two written forms as a requirement: a candidate with one head answers for what is used of it.
Two:
    t: (int: x 0)
    t: (int: x 0)
end: Two
One:
    t: (int: x 4)
end: One
fn: first (@: m Two) int
    return: m\[0]t\x
end: first
fn: second (@: m Two) int
    int: caught 0
    ---
        return: m\[1]t\x
        catch: implements ()
            caught: 1
    ---
    return: 9
end: second
int: code 7
if: first(One) != 4
    code: 81
---
int: outer 0
---
    int: a second(One)
    catch: implements ()
        outer: 1
---
if: code = 7 && outer != 1
    code: 82
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
